<title>QATAR: Commercial Bank of Qatar lifts net, in rights issue.</title>
<headline>Commercial Bank of Qatar lifts net, in rights issue.</headline>
<dateline>DOHA 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			     (million Qatar riyals, rounded)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   50.2     vs	  38.0</p>
<p>    Net interest income	54.7     vs	  42.5</p>
<p>    Other income		 53.3     vs	  42.9</p>
<p>    Provisions		    9.5     vs	   8.7</p>
<p>    Total dividends	    31.6     vs	  26.4</p>
<p>    Total assets (billions)   3.22    vs	   2.66</p>
<p>Full Name : The Commercial Bank of Qatar, QSC.</p>
<p>NOTE: The bank's capital is 105.7 million riyals. The bank decided to pay out the equivalent of 30 percent of its capital in cash dividend. It announced a rights issue of one share for every two held at a premium of 250 riyals. This will raise the banks's capital to 158 million and the shareholders' equity to 400 million riyals.</p>
<p>The bank's shares, nominally valued at 100 riyals, are currently trading at 348 on Qatar's unofficial stock market.</p>
</text>
